# The codebooks of llama.cpp's i-quantized types (T362): what an index of a block stands for. A reader of a GGUF's IQ1,
# IQ2, IQ3 and IQ4 tensors (convert/superblocks.py) looks its groups of 8 or 4 values up here.
#
# The tables are llama.cpp's, of ggml/src/ggml-common.h at the commit 4413a192410fad1f054e9216114087a3e01527a0
# (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp): iq2xxs_grid, iq2xs_grid, iq2s_grid, iq3xxs_grid, iq3s_grid, iq1s_grid and
# kvalues_iq4nl there. They are written otherwise here: a grid's entry is one word there (a value a byte, the first
# value in the lowest byte) and a run of digits here, one digit a value, the first value first; a digit is the place of
# the value among the few a grid has (LEVELS). tests/fork_readers.py holds every entry to llama.cpp's own header.
